abstract:
  A NOMAD plugin providing a NOMAD Action that sends an XPS spectrum stored in NOMAD
  to Galaxy for peak finding, and links the annotated result back into NOMAD as a new
  entry once the Galaxy run completes. Built as an interoperability demonstrator for
  the German node of the European Open Science Cloud (EOSC), showing that a
  NOMAD-stored dataset can be processed by an external workflow platform without
  leaving NOMAD's data model, and that Galaxy can interface with other platforms
  under the EOSC node.
